19 0 obj
<< /A 55 0 R /Alt (Bar charts illustrate pigment content in two plant species, *B. gentionoides* and *V. caruncularis*. The graphs display different parameters: chlorophyll a, chlorophyll b, chlorophyll a+b, chlorophyll a/b ratio, alpha-carotene, beta-carotene, lutein, and total carotenoids. Each chart shows results under various conditions labeled RS, BDS, DS, EDS, and BRS. Error bars and statistical significance letters \(a, b, c\) are included to indicate variation and comparison between groups.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 40 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
20 0 obj
<< /A 56 0 R /Alt <> /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 41 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
21 0 obj
<< /A 57 0 R /Alt (Four-part figure on metabolomic analysis. \(A\) Heatmaps display metabolite levels in *B. gentianoides* and *V. caruncularis* across different treatments, with color indicating concentration. \(B\) PCA plots for both species show clustering based on metabolite profiles. \(C\) Bubble charts highlight significant metabolic pathways, with bubbles sized by enrichment ratio and colored by p-value. \(D\) Venn diagrams illustrate shared and unique metabolites among treatment groups for both species.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 42 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
22 0 obj
<< /A 58 0 R /Alt (Bar charts compare hormone levels in B. gentionoides and V. caruncularis. Charts A and B show ABA levels, C and D show JA, E and F show SA, G and H show ACC. Different treatments \(RS, BDS, DS, EDS, BRS\) are represented. Statistical significance is indicated by letters, showing variance between treatments. Panel H notes a P value of 0.334, indicating no significant difference.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 43 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
23 0 obj
<< /A 59 0 R /Alt (Diagram depicting the physiological responses of two plants, *B. gentianoides* and *V. caruncularis*, across rainy and dry seasons. It highlights changes in relative water content \(RWC\) and various metabolic activities at different stages: RS, BDS, DS, EDS, and BRS. Each plant's adaptation strategies such as sugar increase, stress perception, antioxidant synthesis, and leaf senescence are compared during the rainy and dry seasons, with specific percentages of RWC indicated. Illustrations of both plants are shown.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 47 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
